 format(2000); // "2s"
 ```
 
+### Compound Durations
+
+`parseCompound` sums several parts into a total number of milliseconds. Parts can be separated by spaces, commas, or nothing at all. Every part needs a unit supported by `parse`.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+parseCompound('1h30m'); // 5400000
+```
+
+It throws a `TypeError` if the string is not a valid compound duration; it never returns `NaN`.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
